    "diagnosis": "Papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "This example is arising in a longstanding intra-abdominal lymphatic vascular anomaly, demonstrated on axial T2-weighted, fat-saturated MRI of the abdomen. There are diffuse multiloculated cystic lesions throughout the peritoneum, interdigitating between and displacing loops of small bowel and colon (arrows). Several cystic spaces contain fluid-fluid levels (arrowheads) consistent with layering blood products.",
    "source": "Stephen Broski, MD. Mayo Clinic, Rochester, MN.",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
