  {
    "pkattachmentId": 79949,
    "bookid": 87,
    "chapterId": 210,
    "fileId": 54523,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The splenic section shows extensive ectatic lymphatic vessels with papillary and glomeruloid projections of hobnail endothelial cells. The center of the tumor is fibrotic; the lesion blends in with surrounding splenic tissue at the periphery. WSI information: An 11-years-old boy with a history of asymmetric overgrowth and venous vascular malformation of the left lower extremity was found to have a splenic mass by surveillance imaging. The mass remained relatively stable over the period of 2 years and measured 2.9 cm by the time of the excision. Whole genome sequencing of the patient's germline DNA was negative for pathogenic variants.",
    "source": "Larisa V. Debelenko",
    "copyright": "",
